# sky-net — local settings.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.local.yml --env-file .env.local up --build
#
# Every value is optional. Left as it is, the stack runs on rules only.
# Models are picked in this order: NEBIUS_API_KEY → local Ollama → rules. Whatever a model writes,
# the runtime judges it with the same rules; a model never decides a clearance.
# scripts/dev.sh (no Docker) reads this file when it is saved as .env, finds a local Ollama by
# itself (scripts/resolve_stack.sh) and prints what it picked when it starts.

# ---- Nebius Token Factory ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The key alone is enough: the URL and the nvidia/... model ids are filled in for you.
NEBIUS_API_KEY=

# Override only when needed. The ids match configs/fleet.yaml; `python3 scripts/llm_probe.py`
# lists what your key can reach.
#LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.tokenfactory.nebius.com/v1
#MODEL_NANO=nvidia/Nemotron-3_5-Lightning
#MODEL_SUPER=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
#MODEL_ULTRA=nvidia/Nemotron-3-Ultra-550b-a55b

# Turns thinking off on vLLM-style servers. Not verified on Nebius yet: drop it on a 400.
# With thinking on, the answer arrives in message.reasoning and the client reads content first.
#LLM_REQUEST_EXTRA={"chat_template_kwargs":{"enable_thinking":false}}

# ---- Ollama with scripts/dev.sh (Mac) ---------------------------------------------------
# One Ollama for everything (`ollama pull nemotron-3-nano`). Verified 2026-09-09 on Ollama /v1:
# reasoning_effort=none stops thinking (answers in 0.4–7 s); think=false is ignored on /v1.
#LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#NEBIUS_API_KEY=ollama
#MODEL_NANO=nemotron-3-nano
#MODEL_SUPER=nemotron-3-nano
#MODEL_ULTRA=nemotron-3-nano
#LLM_REQUEST_EXTRA={"reasoning_effort":"none"}

# One server per drone (recommended). Ollama serves nemotron-3-nano one request at a time, so four
# drones sharing one server queue up and time out (7 of 9 drafts in a real run).
#   ollama pull nemotron-3-nano:4b
#   scripts/ollama_fleet.sh start 4    # drones on 11435–11438, the runtime on 11439 (8k context)
#   scripts/ollama_fleet.sh status
#   scripts/ollama_fleet.sh stop 4
# Drone i uses the i-th URL (space-separated, no quotes). With an Ollama URL and no MODEL_NANO the
# drones use nemotron-3-nano:4b. With no MODEL_SUPER only the runtime (11439, else 11434) gets
# LOCAL_SUPER_STANDIN (default nemotron-3-nano:4b) as a local stand-in for Nemotron 3 Super.
#LLM_PER_ASSET_URLS=http://127.0.0.1:11435/v1 http://127.0.0.1:11436/v1 http://127.0.0.1:11437/v1 http://127.0.0.1:11438/v1
#LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#NEBIUS_API_KEY=ollama
#LLM_REQUEST_EXTRA={"reasoning_effort":"none"}

# Arbitration (Ultra) locally needs its own model. The 30B needs the 11434 server started with
# OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=8192: its default 262k context alone takes 26 GB.
#MODEL_ULTRA=nemotron-3-nano:latest

# ---- docker compose with the Mac's Ollama -----------------------------------------------
# compose does not look for running servers the way scripts/dev.sh does. Start the fleet first
# (scripts/ollama_fleet.sh start 4), then uncomment these. Give the model ids: compose defaults to
# Nebius ids, which Ollama does not know. There is no local Ultra, so MODEL_ULTRA= turns it off.
#LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11439/v1
#LLM_URL_1=http://host.docker.internal:11435/v1
#LLM_URL_2=http://host.docker.internal:11436/v1
#LLM_URL_3=http://host.docker.internal:11437/v1
#LLM_URL_4=http://host.docker.internal:11438/v1
#MODEL_NANO=nemotron-3-nano:4b
#MODEL_SUPER=nemotron-3-nano:4b
#MODEL_ULTRA=
#LLM_REQUEST_EXTRA={"reasoning_effort":"none"}

# mlx-lm on the Mac host, reached from the containers.
#LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1

# ---- Model timing -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Seconds to wait for a model. Runtime default 20, drone agents 6 (drone/agent/loop.py build_llm).
#LLM_TIMEOUT_S=6

# Budget for a route draft, counted from the refusal (default 60, both questions together). The
# draft starts the moment a refusal arrives and is collected after the 5.6 s the map spends showing
# it. Reading the map (1,500 tokens) and returning 7 legs took 9 s on an idle 30B; recorded passing
# drafts took 5–19 s, and 19–28 s with four drones on one server, so 6 s would cut every draft.
#DRAFT_TIMEOUT_S=60

# After a server fails to answer, skip drafts for this many seconds (default 30) and use A*.
#DRAFT_BACKOFF_S=30

# Keep every model call as a JSON file; the raw material for tests/fixtures/llm.
#LLM_RECORD_DIR=.run/llm

# Drones re-register their model every 30 s (POST /agents/register → /state.agents). After this
# many ticks without news a drone drops off the list (default 600 = 2 min at 0.2 s per tick).
#AGENT_STALE_TICKS=600

# ---- Route choice -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# When the straight line is refused, the planner draws up to three legal candidates (shortest,
# lowest, clear of other aircraft and incidents) and the drone's Nemotron picks one with a tool
# call (choose_route). Servers without tools get the same question as JSON; with no model the rules
# pick (c when crossing, else a). The runtime judges the pick again: choosing is not clearing.
# Verified 2026-09-11 on Ollama /v1 with nemotron-3-nano:4b: tools and tool_choice=required work,
# answers in 1.1–2.6 s on an idle server. Budget for one choice (tool call plus a JSON retry):
#CHOICE_TIMEOUT_S=10

# A* time limit in seconds for candidates (b) and (c). (a), the shortest, has no limit.
#ROUTE_CANDIDATE_BUDGET_S=12

# ---- Web search and briefing (Tavily) ---------------------------------------------------
# With a key the runtime searches configs/fleet.yaml intake.queries every INTAKE_PERIOD_S seconds
# (default 300) for weather, incidents and flight restrictions. Search results apply only after
# code checks and a person's approval; only official notices apply on the tick. Without a key this
# source is off (/state.intake.sources.tavily = off). An unreachable key writes intake_source_failed
# to the ledger, then intake_source_recovered when Tavily answers again.
TAVILY_API_KEY=
#INTAKE_PERIOD_S=300

# Seconds the Super model gets to read one page. It runs off the world thread; ticks never stop.
#INTAKE_TIMEOUT_S=60

# Pre-flight briefing (configs/fleet.yaml briefing): live Tavily (search, extract, crawl, research)
# with a key, else the recordings in tests/fixtures/tavily, marked "recorded" on the map, in the
# ledger and in the report. A refused key (401) falls back to the recordings. TAVILY_RECORDED=1
# forces the recordings even with a key; 0 never uses them (then no key means no briefing).
#TAVILY_RECORDED=

# Credits per round, shared by the briefing and the search above. Search basic 1, extract 1 per 5
# pages, crawl = map (1 per 10 pages) + extract, research (mini) 4–110 per request. Research bills
# after it finishes, so one call can overshoot; the rest of that round's calls are then skipped.
#TAVILY_BUDGET_PER_ROUND=20

# Keep live answers as files (without the key). Move good ones into tests/fixtures/tavily.
#TAVILY_RECORD_DIR=.run/tavily
#TAVILY_RESEARCH_TIMEOUT_S=120

# Where recorded mode reads from. Point it elsewhere if the image has no tests/ folder.
#TAVILY_FIXTURE_DIR=tests/fixtures/tavily

# Briefing date. Live: today (UTC); recorded: the fixture's as_of. Set it only to replay a past day.
#BRIEFING_DATE=2026-09-22

# ---- Weather (METAR) --------------------------------------------------------------------
# No key needed: aviationweather.gov every METAR_PERIOD_S seconds (default 300). Stations come from
# configs/fleet.yaml intake.metar_stations (KNYC KLGA) unless METAR_STATIONS is set. An official
# observation applies on the tick: gusts past the limits hold takeoffs. Unreachable: the source
# shows off and the ledger gets intake_source_failed; back: on, and intake_source_recovered.
#METAR=off
#METAR_STATIONS=KNYC,KLGA,KJFK
#METAR_PERIOD_S=300

# ---- Intake record ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# What came in (SQLite: items and rules). A restart does not re-read search results or manual
# reports; GET /ledger/report lists them under intake. compose keeps it at /data/intake.sqlite.
#INTAKE_DB=.run/intake.sqlite

# ---- Dispatch (optional: NVIDIA cuOpt on a GPU) -----------------------------------------
# Who flies to which landing site in what order: the operator's job, played by the simulator; the
# runtime is not involved. The default is rule dispatch, so seed 7 plays the same. cuOpt needs a
# GPU: run the cuOpt server (open source, Apache-2.0) on a Nebius AI Cloud GPU instance and give its
# address. A missing, slow or odd answer lets the rules decide that stop and pauses cuOpt for
# CUOPT_BACKOFF_S seconds.
#DISPATCH=cuopt
#CUOPT_URL=http://<nebius-gpu-host>:8000
#CUOPT_TIMEOUT_S=2
#CUOPT_TIME_LIMIT_S=1
#CUOPT_BACKOFF_S=60

# ---- Direct wiring (the comparison world) -----------------------------------------------
# The simulator also runs the same fleet wired straight to the autopilot, for the scoreboard. It
# runs on rules unless DIRECT_LLM=1 (scripts/dev.sh) or DIRECT_LLM_URL (compose); the simulator
# tags each aircraft with DIRECT_MODEL.
#DIRECT_LLM=1
#DIRECT_LLM_URL=https://api.tokenfactory.nebius.com/v1
#DIRECT_MODEL=nvidia/Nemotron-3_5-Lightning

# Seconds between recall checks by a direct agent (default 5). Nothing tells it, so it polls.
#BULLETIN_PERIOD_S=5

# ---- Simulation -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Seconds per tick. Lower is faster.
TICK_SECONDS=0.2
